Here's a Java solution:

```java
public static boolean isThreePower(int n) {
    if (n < 0) {
        // Negative numbers cannot be represented as a power of 3
        return false;
    }
    // The largest power of 3 that fits within the given integer range is 3^(31 - 1) = 2,147,483,647
    // If n is greater than this value, it cannot be a power of 3 either
    if (n > Integer.MAX_VALUE / 3) {
        return false;
    }
    // A number is a power of 3 if and only if its logarithm base 3 is an integer
    return (Math.log10(n) / Math.log10(3)) % 1 == 0;
}
```

